      "hints": [
        "An $x$-axis point has $y=0$.",
        "Factorise $x^2-4x-12$.",
        "Complete both squares in the circle equation."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "$y=0$ gives $(x-6)(x+2)=0$, so $A(-2,0)$ and $B(6,0)$.",
        "The equation becomes $(x-2)^2+(y+3)^2=25$.",
        "Hence the centre is $(2,-3)$ and the radius is $5$."
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_p1_t_coordinate_geometry_m05_l01_cpq07_p02",
      "difficulty": 3,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_coordinate_geometry",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_coordinate_geometry_m05_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Add the two equations to eliminate $y$.",
        "Substitute the value of $x$ into either equation.",
        "$C$ and $T$ have the same $x$-coordinate."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Adding gives $8x=16$, so $x=2$; substitution gives $y=16/3$.",
        "Thus $T=(2,16/3)$.",
        "$CT=16/3+3=25/3$."
      ]
    }
  ]
